sections.text:
Mixing units is the most common error. Pressure may be in bar, psi or Pa; permeability in mD or m²; volume in barrels or m³. Convert before you calculate.

Other common mistakes are:
using a fluid property correlation outside its valid range;
confusing reservoir rock properties with fluid properties;
treating a simulation result as exact;
forgetting uncertainty in reserves and forecasts;
ignoring economics, safety and environmental limits until the end;
memorising formulas without knowing their assumptions;
copying a rule from a code or regulation without checking the edition and the country;
not checking your own handbook for degree and registration requirements.

State your assumptions. An examiner needs to see how you reached the answer.
